-- Plots v2's flip (V2.0, #459): the planned nodes, re-planned for the 16600
-- world.
--
-- Every zone moved out to its v2 ring (urban to r2160, the suburb to r3600,
-- rural to r6100, the wilds to r8300) and took its v2 layout, so the plan
-- changed everywhere past the urban grid's first three rings of blocks: the
-- spawn densities are per area, so the rural ring's woods, branches,
-- outcrops and veins cover the bigger ring, the urban and suburban clay and
-- branches follow the new canal bank and parks, and the wilds grow on new
-- land. About 18,000 nodes, from about 13,200.
--
-- This replaces every planned row rather than adding to them, as RW1's
-- 20261122_001_rural_widens_nodes.sql did: every node of a planned type goes,
-- from that re-plan and from the partial re-plans since (20261125, 20261126,
-- 20261201, 20261205 and 20261207), and the new plan comes in. The seeded
-- grass isn't planned, and stays, moved by the first set's
-- 20261220_001_plots_v2_flip.sql. Nothing a player owns is a node, so no
-- owner loses one; a node half gathered starts over.
--
-- The rows come from the ignored test `print_new_nodes` run with
-- `PRINT_ALL_NODES=1`, and `the_migration_writes_the_default_plan` checks
-- they still match the plan.
--
--   clay_bank in suburban: 52
--   clay_bank in urban: 69
--   clay_bank in wilderness: 398
--   copper_vein in wilderness: 995
--   fallen_branches in rural: 1143
--   fallen_branches in suburban: 104
--   fallen_branches in wilderness: 2986
--   iron_vein in rural: 152
--   iron_vein in wilderness: 796
--   old_growth in wilderness: 5972
--   reed_bed in wilderness: 597
--   rock_outcrop in rural: 457
--   rock_outcrop in wilderness: 1991
--   tin_vein in wilderness: 398
--   tree in rural: 1905
DELETE FROM resource_nodes
WHERE resource_type IN ('tree', 'old_growth', 'fallen_branches', 'rock_outcrop', 'iron_vein', 'copper_vein',
                        'tin_vein', 'clay_bank', 'reed_bed');

ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
